# A 256-byte struct assignment, which selectMemoryCopy will not spell out one
# chunk at a time - MAX_UNROLLED_COPY caps that at 128 bytes, past which the
# right shape is a loop or a call to memcpy and neither exists here yet.
# Delete this line once a large copy has a rule.
copyBig
# The same struct passed by value, which is a second refusal on top of the
# copy: the IR hands the callee an address, the SysV ABI says the callee reads
# bytes on its own stack, and the two halves of the convention do not meet.
sumBigByValue
